    "aboveFold": true
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 5,
   "tag": "p",
   "landmarks": [
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 585,
   "text": "I remember being amazed watching videos of the moon landing—but also confused. The cars, telephones, TVs, and computers of my childhood were worlds more advanced than anything my parents had as kids. But with space, the normal order of things was reversed: My parents grew up exhilarated by Apollo missions to places no man had gone before, while I was watching the space shuttle take astronauts a li",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
