    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 7,
   "tag": "p×14",
   "class": "wp-block-paragraph",
   "landmarks": [
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 4251,
   "text": "People living in the 1960s thought the moon landing was just the beginning. By 2024, they’d have imagined, there would be a permanent moon base, lots of space tourism, and even people walking around on other planets.\nAs it turns out, the 1960s were a fluke. It was the height of the Cold War and “desperate times call for desperate measures” justified all kinds of unusual behaviors—including spendin",
